@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #1F3864
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #1F3864
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F3864
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold
skinparam ParticipantStereotypeFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #1F3864
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #9AA3B5
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #D5D9E0
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F3F6FC
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #9AA3B5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C98A2B
skinparam NoteFontColor #3A2A00
skinparam NoteFontSize 11
skinparam MessageFontName Menlo
skinparam MessageFontSize 11
hide footbox

title Issue #58, Complete a cart when an item ran out of stock: UML Sequence Diagram

actor Storefront <<actor>>
participant "POST /store/carts/:id/complete" as Route <<boundary>> #2E7D32
participant "completeCartWorkflow" as WF <<control>>
participant "reserveInventoryStep" as Step <<control>>
participant "InventoryModuleService" as Inv <<entity>> #2E7D32

Storefront -> Route : POST /store/carts/:id/complete
activate Route

Route -> WF : run via workflow engine\n({ input: { id }, throwOnError: false })
activate WF
note right of WF
  <b><color:#B8761B>(1) Errors come back, not thrown</color></b>
  throwOnError: false makes the engine return
  the error, so the route decides the response.
end note

WF -> Step : reserveInventoryStep(items)
activate Step
Step -> Inv : createReservationItems(items)
activate Inv
Inv -> Inv : ensureInventoryLevels(items,\n{ validateQuantityAtLocation: true })

alt available_quantity < quantity
  Inv -[#2E7D32]-> Step : <color:#2E7D32><b>throw MedusaError(NOT_ALLOWED, "Not enough stock...",</b></color>\n<color:#2E7D32><b>INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY)</b></color>
  deactivate Inv
  note right of Inv
    <b><color:#B8761B>(2) Code added at the source</color></b>
    Same type and message as before. Attaching the
    existing INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY code is what lets
    the route tell it apart from other NOT_ALLOWED errors.
  end note
end

Step --> WF : step fails
deactivate Step
WF -> WF : compensate earlier steps\n(delete order and links)
note right of WF
  <b><color:#B8761B>(3) Cart stays usable</color></b>
  Compensation rolls back the order, so the
  cart is still incomplete and can be fixed.
end note
WF --> Route : { errors: [{ error }] }
deactivate WF

Route -> Route : refetchCart(id)

alt <color:#2E7D32><b>error.code in statusOKErrorCodes (new)</b></color>
  Route -[#2E7D32]-> Storefront : <color:#2E7D32><b>200 { type: "cart", cart, error: { message, name, type } }</b></color>
  note right of Route
    <b><color:#B8761B>(4) Same shape as payment errors</color></b>
    The storefront already handles type "cart" for
    payment errors, so it can now show which item is
    out of stock and let the shopper remove it.
  end note
else other errors (e.g. promotion limit, also NOT_ALLOWED)
  Route --> Storefront : 400 { type, message, code }
end
deactivate Route

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid arrow | Synchronous call |
  | dashed arrow | Return or thrown error |
  | grey bar | Activation (object busy) |
  | Navy box | Existing code, unchanged |
  | <back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> Green box </color></back> / <color:#2E7D32><b>green text</b></color> | New or modified for #58 |
  | <<boundary>> / <<control>> / <<entity>> | HTTP layer / workflow logic / module holding the data |
  | <back:#FFF8E6> Amber note </back> | Design decision callout |
endlegend
@enduml
